Description: A search only filters the Search page, not Browse
 The Search and Browse tabs share one track table (LibraryTable_Singleton),
 so a query typed on the Search page kept filtering the list in Browse and
 the other tracks in the folder could not be seen. WSearchLineEdit now
 parks its query when the Search page is hidden (a hide while the window
 stays up; closing or minimising the window is ignored), re-runs the search
 with an empty query so Browse shows the whole folder, and puts the query
 back when the Search page is shown again, run over whatever is selected
 then. If that view has no search (box disabled) the query stays parked.
